## Introduction

Derive consequences from facts, combine conditions, and distinguish a model from its displayed atoms.

Use a local Livebook **Standalone** runtime with Elixir 1.20 / OTP 29 on a
[platform with an available bundle](../../README.md#platforms-and-installation).
The setup cell installs this checkout, its bundled clingo runtime, and Kino.
No separate clingo installation, compiler, or environment variables are needed.
The first Kino installation needs network access; the examples use local data.

Choose **Evaluate all**, or evaluate cells in order from the top. Worked examples
check their stated answers; update those checks when editing ASP. Exercise
templates are deliberately incomplete. File sections create disposable workspaces;
download your edits before running their cleanup cell.

